  "note": "Mouthpiece at the top, slide travelling down (orient: \"horizontal\" gives the usual side view, slide to the right). The body (mouthpiece, bell section and bell) is always drawn; dotted rails mark where the slide travels. Spacing follows the real instrument: the slide hand is level with the bell rim at 3rd position. Seven slide keys, pos1 to pos7, are hidden until a fingering presses one: a fingering lists exactly one position. Each position carries its number as a tag. With the hints render option, light dotted marks show the hand positions the slide has passed (keys with showWith appear only while one of those positions is in use).",
